---
title: Roast pork tenderloin
servings: 6
tags: [american, pork, weeknight, quick]
cuisine: american
time: 30 minutes
source: Best Juicy Pork Tenderloin by Adam Gallagher, Inspired Taste, https://www.inspiredtaste.net/10767/simply-seared-pork-tenderloin-recipe/
---

Heat the oven to 425°F.

Trim the @pork tenderloins{2}(1 to 1 1/2 lb each) and cut away the silverskin.
Pat dry and salt generously with @salt{} and @black pepper{}.

Heat 1 tbsp of the @canola oil{2%tbsp} in a #cast-iron skillet{} over medium
heat. Brown the pork ~{2%minutes} a side, then sprinkle over the
@spice rub{1%tbsp}(or up to 2 tbsp).

Move the pan to the oven and roast ~{15%minutes}, until the thickest part
reads 145°F to 150°F.

Rest ~{5%minutes} to ~{10%minutes}, then slice.

== Pan sauce ==

Set the skillet back over medium heat. Add the @dry white wine{3/4%cup}(or broth or cider),
scrape up the browned bits, and simmer until halved.

Stir in the @unsalted butter{1%tbsp} and spoon over the sliced pork.

> Any rub works, fresh or dried; check the pork from 10 minutes.
